sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant DR as Driver App
    participant WS as WebSocket Gateway
    participant API as Node.js API
    participant AUTH as JWT/Auth Guard
    participant DB as Supabase PostgreSQL
    participant M as MongoDB Telemetry
    participant OPS as Dispatcher Dashboard
    participant C as Customer App
    participant MON as Telemetry Monitor

    DR->>WS: Open authenticated WebSocket
    WS->>AUTH: Validate driver JWT
    AUTH-->>WS: Driver identity and permissions
    WS-->>DR: Connection accepted with sessionId

    DR->>WS: Subscribe to assigned trip
    WS->>API: Verify driver-trip ownership
    API->>DB: Read assignment and trip state
    DB-->>API: Valid assignment
    API-->>WS: Subscription authorized
    WS-->>DR: Trip telemetry channel ready

    loop Every approximately 5 seconds
        DR->>WS: GPS point(eventId, coordinates, timestamp)
        WS->>API: Validate event envelope
        API->>AUTH: Confirm session and driver identity
        AUTH-->>API: Authorized driver
        API->>API: Validate coordinates, timestamp, and speed
        API->>M: Insert telemetry with eventId and timestamp
        M-->>API: Accepted or duplicate event
        API->>WS: Publish latest accepted point
        WS-->>OPS: Live driver location and freshness
        WS-->>C: Customer tracking update
        API-->>DR: Ack eventId
    end

    alt Driver temporarily loses network
        DR->>DR: Store bounded local event queue
        DR->>WS: Reconnect with session token
        WS->>AUTH: Revalidate JWT
        AUTH-->>WS: Session restored
        DR->>WS: Replay queued eventIds
        WS->>API: Validate timestamp and deduplicate
        API->>M: Insert only unseen points
        API-->>DR: Ack accepted or rejected events
    else Point is late or out of order
        API->>M: Compare device timestamp with latest point
        M-->>API: Older point detected
        API-->>DR: Ack as stored, not current position
        API-->>WS: Do not move current marker backward
    else Invalid or unauthorized point
        API-->>DR: Reject with telemetry error
        API->>MON: Record security or data-quality event
    end

    MON->>M: Check latest telemetry timestamp
    M-->>MON: Last accepted point and age
    alt Telemetry exceeds stale threshold
        MON->>DB: Record driver telemetry stale state
        MON->>WS: Publish driver.stale
        WS-->>OPS: Show last known point and age
        WS-->>C: Show tracking unavailable or stale
    else Telemetry is fresh
        MON->>WS: Publish driver.active
        WS-->>OPS: Show active location state
    end

    Note over M: Telemetry uses geospatial indexing and a seven-day TTL in the scale phase.
    Note over OPS: Real-time messages are eventually consistent.
    Note over C: REST remains authoritative for booking state.
